The Dropbear SSH client in term51
=================================

The file dropbearmulti in this folder of the package is the client side of
Dropbear 2026.94 for BlackBerry 10: ssh (Dropbear's dbclient), scp,
dropbearkey and dropbearconvert in one program. There is no SSH server in
it. term51 builds it from upstream Dropbear at its 2026.94 release (the
submodule third_party/dropbear) with term51's changes for QNX: about a
hundred lines in tools/dropbear/qnx.patch, and the settings, the build
script and the way to build the same bytes again in tools/dropbear/qnx/.

Dropbear is under an MIT-style licence: see LICENSE here, which also names
the parts taken from elsewhere (scp and a few helpers from OpenSSH, BSD
licence). Its cryptography is libtomcrypt and libtommath, released into the
public domain: see libtomcrypt.LICENSE and libtommath.LICENSE. The program
also contains helper functions of LLVM's compiler-rt (Apache License 2.0
with LLVM exceptions), which the toolchain links in.

term51 runs it as a separate program, by the names ssh, dbclient, scp,
dropbearkey and dropbearconvert at the end of the shell's PATH.

Two things to know when using it: keys are in Dropbear's own file format
(dropbearkey makes one; dropbearconvert brings an OpenSSH key over), and
the algorithms based on SHA-1 are switched on beside the modern ones,
because older servers, QNX 6.5's among them, know no others.
